  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Independent South Building: full mapped cruciform two-storey body, banded red brick and pale terracotta, canted central bays, green-gray mansard roofs with pedimented dormers, four end pavilions and paired tall chimneys, raised decorated drum and broad dark copper dome. Reconstruct a lower west service entrance recess/soffit and three approach treads; entrance bearing and thresholds are approximate. Preserve the independent planetarium, Altazimuth Pavilion and all other campus buildings. Exterior only: no furnished galleries, working instruments, copied inscriptions, sculpture portraits or signs.",
    "identityBasis": "Shared campus Q192988 plus unique way268533442/native35184640622274, the mapped cross-shaped South Building. Parent has no mapped height and no contained building_part records in this extract. Own anchor raw[59.5,110], X east/Z south, heading0 baked into the mapped footprint. East/west photo labels and cross arms guide orientation. Four repeated roof/stack treatments and hidden north/south elevations are reconstructed; lower west service-door assignment is approximate. Only this parent footprint is owned; the separately mapped planetarium and every other campus building remain independent.",
    "heightBasis": "No mapped height. Working wall7.8m/mansard10.7m, end pavilions12.4m/chimneys14m, upper core11.3m/drum14m/dome18.8m and simple finial20.3m are picture-led estimates. Banded facade/window/pilaster/dormer inventories, hidden roof junctions, end repetition and dome profile are simplified. Shared stone graph tinted terracotta substitutes for molded ornament; slate is tinted green-gray. The historic principal eastern entrance is at first-floor level; exact hillside access is unverified and the lower west door is a reconstructed service-entry proxy, not a surveyed principal entrance.",
    "terrainBasis": "Existing standard Protomaps20261020/Mapzen201x201/6m Observatory extract reused. Uncovered western approach internal[-16.8,0] fixes datum44.36029666666667m, working lower floor0.6m above it with three0.2m treads. Original hill slopes across the cross-shaped footprint; closed foundation follows its minimum boundary grade. Only the occupied parent footprint cuts ground. Approximate native exterior fit reviewed on the original hill; boundary grades -0.257..+1.332m leave a modest lower-side base and slight uphill burial. Exact historic retaining terraces, principal first-floor access and thresholds remain approximate. No bespoke terrain acquisition or broad flattening.",
